### Inside the band: year to year

Each row of years 4 and 5 assumes the year before's row in its thread (one grade back), so it opens as a retrieval
task inside day 2 of its unit.

| Thread | Year 3 row (unit, course days) | Year 4 row that picks it up (unit) | Year 5 row that picks it up (unit) | What changes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Choosing | mu-g3-choose (unit 1, days 1 to 16) | mu-g4-choose (unit 5): the class's skill is a reason for a pick | mu-g5-choose (unit 9) retrieves mu-g4-choose (unit 5, days 65 to 80): a pick backed with evidence | Setting, then skill, then evidence |
| Responding | mu-g3-respond (unit 1, days 1 to 16) | mu-g4-respond (unit 5): why the setting changes the response | mu-g5-respond (unit 9) retrieves mu-g4-respond (unit 5, days 65 to 80): a written response with evidence, history and culture | Described, then explained, then argued with evidence |
| Inventing | mu-g3-invent (unit 2, days 17 to 28) | mu-g4-invent (unit 6): harmony over a drone, an accompaniment | mu-g5-invent (unit 10) retrieves mu-g4-invent (unit 6, days 81 to 92): easy chords, a historical setting | A chosen tonality, then a drone and accompaniment, then chords tied to a setting |
| Expression | mu-g3-express (unit 2, days 17 to 28) | mu-g4-express (unit 6): tone color, explained | mu-g5-express (unit 10) retrieves mu-g4-express (unit 6, days 81 to 92): articulation | Loudness and speed, then tone color, then articulation |
| Writing it down | mu-g3-document (unit 3, days 31 to 46) | mu-g4-document (unit 7): organized ideas, a simple harmony part | mu-g5-document (unit 11) retrieves mu-g4-document (unit 7, days 95 to 110): developed ideas, two-chord harmony | One melody, then a harmony part, then two chords |
| Revising | mu-g3-revise (unit 3, days 31 to 46) | mu-g4-revise (unit 7): a dated revision log, growth | mu-g5-revise (unit 11) retrieves mu-g4-revise (unit 7, days 95 to 110): a reason for each change | A change list, then a log over time, then reasons |
| Reading | mu-g3-read (unit 4, days 49 to 64) | mu-g4-read (unit 8): timing, pitch and form explained; time signatures | mu-g5-read (unit 12) retrieves mu-g4-read (unit 8, days 113 to 128): harmony, standard notation as the default | Picture and standard, then either, then standard |
| Performing | mu-g3-perform (unit 4, days 49 to 64) | mu-g4-perform (unit 8): interpretation for the genre | mu-g5-perform (unit 12) retrieves mu-g4-perform (unit 8, days 113 to 128): growth shown in a rehearsal log | Class criteria, then shared criteria and genre, then growth over weeks |

