Each hand-on above is answered at both ends in data/progressions/arts.csv (the grade 6 rows' `assumes` cells).
Music 6 to 8 picks these rows up in its grade 6 units 1 to 4 (its Seams, "Picked up from Music, grades 3 to 5"); the music expert read checks the two tables against each other.

## Models carried

| Model | Where it comes from | Introduced or first used here | Used again here |
|---|---|---|---|
| listening-log | Music K to 2 (mu-k-choose, model_out; grade 2 in mu-g2-choose) | Unit 1: a page per piece heard, now with the setting (what it is for, where it is heard) and the class's reason for a pick | Unit 5 (the class's skill as a reason, mu-g4-choose), unit 9 (evidence from the music, mu-g5-choose); every unit adds pages |
| describe-interpret-judge | Music K to 2 (mu-k-respond, model_out; grade 2 in mu-g2-respond) | Unit 1: listen, describe form and elements, say how the setting shapes the response, score with a set checklist, connect | Unit 5 (explained, with the cultural setting, mu-g4-respond), unit 9 (written with evidence, mu-g5-respond); every listen as review |
| idea-bank | Music K to 2 (mu-k-invent, model_out; grade 2 in mu-g2-invent) | Unit 2: the class's bundle of improvised idea cards and sound-only recordings, each with its tonality, meter and setting | Unit 6 (drone and accompaniment ideas, mu-g4-invent), unit 10 (chord-backed ideas, mu-g5-invent); each composing unit draws from it |
| expression-map | Music K to 2 (mu-k-express, model_out; grade 2 in mu-g2-express) | Unit 2: a strip of the piece with loudness and speed marks, one per reading | Unit 6 (tone color added, mu-g4-express), unit 10 (articulation added, mu-g5-express); each concert unit's plan as review |
| notation-ladder | Music K to 2 (mu-k-document, model_out; grade 2 in mu-g2-document) | Unit 3: picture notation, then standard notation of rhythm and a pentatonic tune, rung by rung | Unit 7 (a simple harmony part, mu-g4-document), unit 11 (two-chord harmony, mu-g5-document) |
| critique-protocol | Music K to 2 (mu-k-revise, model_out; grade 2 in mu-g2-revise) | Unit 3: describe what you hear, ask about a choice, suggest one change tied to the class checklist, with a change list | Unit 7 (a dated revision log, mu-g4-revise), unit 11 (a reason for each change, mu-g5-revise); every critique day as review |
| rhythm-syllables | Music K to 2 (mu-k-read, model_out; grade 2 in mu-g2-read) | Unit 4: syllables and beat counts, then note values as parts of a whole bar | Unit 8 (equal note values in a bar, time signatures, mu-g4-read), unit 12 (mixed values added within a bar, mu-g5-read); every warm-up echo as review |
| practice-plan | Music K to 2 (mu-k-perform, model_out; grade 2 in mu-g2-perform) | Unit 4: the practice card: find the weak spot, name the strategy (slow then up to speed, in parts, hands only), take it again | Unit 8 (shared criteria, solo and group, mu-g4-perform), unit 12 (a rehearsal log with kept takes, mu-g5-perform) |

All eight come in from grade 2 (the mu-g3 rows' model_in) and go on to grade 6 (the mu-g6 rows' model_in).

