r rhythm and short tune read and played; MU:Pr4.2.3c, a written item on the reading day: one way the song's setting shapes how it is sung; MU:Pr5.1.3a, a kept card: a recorded class take marked on the shared checklist with one point of feedback; MU:Pr5.1.3b, a guide look-for on the kept practice card: a weak spot, its strategy and the take before and after; MU:Pr6.1.3a, a guide look-for at the concert: the part sung or played accurately and with the planned expression; MU:Pr6.1.3b, a guide look-for at the concert: performer manners in the group's turn and audience manners in the others'. Each item is marked met, partly or not yet. Out: time signatures (grade 4); solo performance (grade 4, offered here only as a choice). Tools: the form map, the practice card, the shared checklist, reading cards, Curio Class's own; a rhythm reading tool or the printed cards. Free path: the voice and printed cards. Once-a-week path: 7 sessions | Last in the year because the concert ends it and because reading note values as parts of a whole bar waits for math grade 3 unit 6 (days 92 to 114, school weeks 19 to 23); this unit starts in week 25. The year-end check sits before it (week 24); its own two check days in weeks 31 and 32 are its assessment. The rhythm-syllables and practice-plan models are retrieved here | Candidate: the concert program written by the class as a kept card, read by the sensitivity agent | Family yes for any showing outside class; a student's name is printed only as the student chooses. Every part has a solo or doubled version for the home room and a group version for a student who will not sing alone. Hazards and controls: voice rest and water in each rehearsal; no loud drum near an ear; the concert space cleared and steps checked. Agent reads: sensitivity; safety (hands-on). |
