{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '2', 'skill_id': 'mu-g2-read', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.2.2a; MU:Pr4.2.2b', 'assumes': 'mu-g1-read', 'hands_on': 'mu-g3-read', 'model_in': 'rhythm-syllables', 'model_out': 'rhythm-syllables', 'words': 'tonality; meter; major; minor; rhythm pattern; melody pattern', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Learn songs from more than one culture and show whether each is major or minor and moves in twos or threes, then read and play rhythm and melody patterns from picture or standard notation. Rhythms are taught by beat counts and a spoken counting system. What changes: tonality and meter are named, and melody patterns are read as well as rhythms. Assessed by a read-and-play task scored on a three-line guide. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '2', 'skill_id': 'mu-g2-express', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.3.2a; MU:Re8.1.2a', 'assumes': 'mu-g1-express', 'hands_on': 'mu-g3-express', 'model_in': 'expression-map', 'model_out': 'expression-map', 'words': 'tempo; dynamics; concept; intent; creator; performer', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Perform a song with planned loud, soft, fast and slow parts, then listen to two performers and say how each one's choices show what the music means. What changes: qualities beyond loudness and speed are tied to a creator's intent. Assessed by a performance and a spoken reason scored on a three-line guide."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '2', 'skill_id': 'mu-g2-perform', 'standard': 'MU:Pr5.1.2a; MU:Pr5.1.2b; MU:Pr6.1.2a; MU:Pr6.1.2b', 'assumes': 'mu-g1-perform', 'hands_on': 'mu-g3-perform', 'model_in': 'practice-plan', 'model_out': 'practice-plan', 'words': 'criteria; accurate; expressive; effective; strategy; rehearse', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Score a class performance with a short checklist, practice one hard spot with a named strategy such as slow, then up to speed, and perform for a purpose such as a morning song. What changes: the child chooses the strategy and judges with set criteria. Assessed by a performance scored on a three-line guide (accurate, expressive, fits the purpose).'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '2', 'skill_id': 'mu-g2-choose', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.1.2a; MU:Re7.1.2a; MU:Cn10.1.2a', 'assumes': 'mu-g1-choose', 'hands_on': 'mu-g3-choose', 'model_in': 'listening-log', 'model_out': 'listening-log', 'words': 'interest; purpose; explain; choose; knowledge; varied', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Choose music for a class purpose from a listening menu and explain the pick, and tell how something the child likes or has done shapes the choice. What changes: the child explains a choice in words, where grade 1 showed and discussed it. Assessed by a short spoken or written reason scored on a three-line guide.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '2', 'skill_id': 'mu-g2-respond', 'standard': 'MU:Re7.2.2a; MU:Re9.1.2a; MU:Cn11.1.2a', 'assumes': 'mu-g1-respond', 'hands_on': 'mu-g3-respond', 'model_in': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'model_out': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'words': 'concept; purpose; judge; taste; connect; subject', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Listen for how a piece's beat, tune or speed suits its purpose, judge it for that purpose by taste and expression, and connect it to another art or a school subject. What changes: the child describes how a music concept serves a purpose, where grade 1 only showed it. Assessed by a short listen-and-describe response scored on a three-line guide. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'mu-g3-invent', 'standard': 'MU:Cr1.1.3a; MU:Cr1.1.3b', 'assumes': 'mu-g2-invent', 'hands_on': 'mu-g4-invent', 'model_in': 'idea-bank', 'model_out': 'idea-bank', 'words': 'improvise; setting; purpose; choose; fits; tonality', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Improvise rhythm and melody ideas, say how they fit a purpose and a setting, then invent ideas in a tonality or meter the child chooses. What changes: the child explains the fit and chooses the tonality or meter. Assessed by a performance and a spoken reason scored on a short rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'mu-g3-document', 'standard': 'MU:Cr2.1.3a; MU:Cr2.1.3b', 'assumes': 'mu-g2-document', 'hands_on': 'mu-g4-document', 'model_in': 'notation-ladder', 'model_out': 'notation-ladder', 'words': 'piece; purpose; rhythm; melody; standard notation; picture notation', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Make up a short piece for a purpose (a game song, a goodnight tune) and write its rhythm and melody in picture or standard notation, or record it. What changes: ideas become a piece with a stated purpose. Assessed by a documented piece, played with its purpose said, scored on a short rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'mu-g3-revise', 'standard': 'MU:Cr3.1.3a; MU:Cr3.2.3a', 'assumes': 'mu-g2-revise', 'hands_on': 'mu-g4-revise', 'model_in': 'critique-protocol', 'model_out': 'critique-protocol', 'words': 'criteria; judge; record; changes; audience; intent', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Improve a class piece with a checklist the teacher and class set, mark the changes on the page, and share it with an audience, saying how it shows what the child meant. What changes: class criteria guide the changes and an audience hears the result. Assessed by a revised piece with a recorded change list, shared with an audience with its intent described, scored on a short rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'mu-g3-read', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.2.3a; MU:Pr4.2.3b; MU:Pr4.2.3c', 'assumes': 'mu-g2-read', 'hands_on': 'mu-g4-read', 'model_in': 'rhythm-syllables', 'model_out': 'rhythm-syllables', 'words': 'structure; section; rhythm; short tune; notation; context', 'cross_subject': 'math:3.NF.A.1 (a note value is a part of a whole bar)', 'notes': 'Map the form of a song the class will perform, read and play its rhythms and short tune from picture and standard notation, and talk about how where and why people sing it shapes the performance. Note values are placed after the unit on fractions as parts of a whole. What changes: whole tunes are read in picture and standard notation, and the setting of a performance is described. Assessed by a form map, a read-and-play task and a written description of the setting, scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'mu-g3-express', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.3.3a; MU:Re8.1.3a', 'assumes': 'mu-g2-express', 'hands_on': 'mu-g4-express', 'model_in': 'expression-map', 'model_out': 'expression-map', 'words': 'reading; interpret; loudness; speed; intent; performer', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Try a song with different loudness and speed and pick the version that carries its meaning, then describe how a recorded performer uses the same tools. What changes: the child compares readings by different performers, where grade 2 named qualities in one. Assessed by a performance and a short description scored on a short rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'mu-g3-perform', 'standard': 'MU:Pr5.1.3a; MU:Pr5.1.3b; MU:Pr6.1.3a; MU:Pr6.1.3b', 'assumes': 'mu-g2-perform', 'hands_on': 'mu-g4-perform', 'model_in': 'practice-plan', 'model_out': 'practice-plan', 'words': 'ensemble; criteria; polish; manners; audience; venue', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Score a class ensemble take for accuracy with a shared checklist, rehearse the weak spots, and perform for an audience with the manners of a performer and a listener. What changes: ensemble work, class criteria and audience manners. Assessed by a performance, a take judged on class criteria and a self-check, with performer and audience manners observed, scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: a solo or doubled version is always offered.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'mu-g3-choose', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.1.3a; MU:Re7.1.3a; MU:Cn10.1.3a', 'assumes': 'mu-g2-choose', 'hands_on': 'mu-g4-choose', 'model_in': 'listening-log', 'model_out': 'listening-log', 'words': 'setting; purpose; choose; reflect; knowledge; audience', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Choose a piece for the class to perform and present the reasons (what it is for, where it will be sung, what the class knows), and tell how it fits the student's own interests. What changes: setting joins interest and purpose as a reason for choosing music to perform. Assessed by a listening-log entry with a reason scored on a short rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '3', 'skill_id': 'mu-g3-respond', 'standard': 'MU:Re7.2.3a; MU:Re9.1.3a; MU:Cn11.1.3a', 'assumes': 'mu-g2-respond', 'hands_on': 'mu-g4-respond', 'model_in': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'model_out': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'words': 'structure; element; setting; criteria; fit; connect', 'cross_subject': 'ela:SL.3.1 (class talk about what was heard)', 'notes': "Listen to a piece, describe how its form, its elements and where it is heard shape the student's response, score it with a set checklist, and connect it to another art or subject. What changes: set criteria and the personal or social setting enter the judging, where grade 2 judged by taste and expression. Assessed by a listen-and-describe response scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'mu-g4-invent', 'standard': 'MU:Cr1.1.4a; MU:Cr1.1.4b', 'assumes': 'mu-g3-invent', 'hands_on': 'mu-g5-invent', 'model_in': 'idea-bank', 'model_out': 'idea-bank', 'words': 'harmony; accompaniment; related; explain; setting; drone', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Improvise rhythms and tunes with a simple harmony part over a drone, say how they fit a stated purpose, and make up a short accompaniment in a given key and meter. What changes: harmony and accompaniment join rhythm and melody. Assessed by a performance with a spoken reason, scored on a short rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'mu-g4-document', 'standard': 'MU:Cr2.1.4a; MU:Cr2.1.4b', 'assumes': 'mu-g3-document', 'hands_on': 'mu-g5-document', 'model_in': 'notation-ladder', 'model_out': 'notation-ladder', 'words': 'arrange; compose; organized; context; harmony; notation', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Play ideas chosen and organized for improvising, arranging or composing, say what each is for, and write down rhythm, melody and a simple harmony part. What changes: organizing and explaining join documenting, and simple harmony is written down, where grade 3 documented one melody. Assessed by a documented piece and a spoken or written reason, scored on a rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'mu-g4-revise', 'standard': 'MU:Cr3.1.4a; MU:Cr3.2.4a', 'assumes': 'mu-g3-revise', 'hands_on': 'mu-g5-revise', 'model_in': 'critique-protocol', 'model_out': 'critique-protocol', 'words': 'growth; shared criteria; revise; record; audience; explain', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Keep a revision log for one piece against shared criteria, recording each change and the date, then share the finished piece with an audience and say how it shows the student's aim. What changes: changes are kept over time and shown as growth, where grade 3 kept a change list. Assessed by a portfolio entry with before and after versions, shared with an audience with its intent explained, scored on a rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'mu-g4-read', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.2.4a; MU:Pr4.2.4b; MU:Pr4.2.4c', 'assumes': 'mu-g3-read', 'hands_on': 'mu-g5-read', 'model_in': 'rhythm-syllables', 'model_out': 'rhythm-syllables', 'words': 'timing; pitch; form; time signature; notation; culture', 'cross_subject': 'math:4.NF.A.1 (equal note values, such as two quarters in one half)', 'notes': 'Mark the rhythm, pitch and form of a piece the class will perform, read and play it from picture or standard notation, and explain how its social and cultural setting shapes how it is sung or played. Equal note values are shown as equal parts of a bar. What changes: elements are named and explained, and setting is explained rather than described. Assessed by a marked score and form map, a read-and-play task and a short explanation, scored on a rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'mu-g4-express', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.3.4a; MU:Re8.1.4a', 'assumes': 'mu-g3-express', 'hands_on': 'mu-g5-express', 'model_in': 'expression-map', 'model_out': 'expression-map', 'words': 'interpretive choice; tone color; loudness; speed; intent; explain', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Plan the loudness, speed and tone color of a song on an expression map and perform it, then explain how a recorded performer's choices carry the music's meaning. What changes: tone color joins loudness and speed, and explaining replaces describing. Assessed by a performance and a spoken reason scored on a rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'mu-g4-perform', 'standard': 'MU:Pr5.1.4a; MU:Pr5.1.4b; MU:Pr6.1.4a; MU:Pr6.1.4b', 'assumes': 'mu-g3-perform', 'hands_on': 'mu-g5-perform', 'model_in': 'practice-plan', 'model_out': 'practice-plan', 'words': 'solo; group; shared criteria; interpretation; genre; manners', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Judge group and solo takes with a shared checklist, rehearse to fix accuracy and expression, and perform alone or in a group with the interpretation and manners the setting and genre call for. What changes: interpretation is tied to the genre, where grade 3 tied manners to the venue. Assessed by a performance, a take judged on class criteria and a self-check, with performer and audience manners observed, scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: a solo or doubled version is always offered.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'mu-g4-choose', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.1.4a; MU:Re7.1.4a; MU:Cn10.1.4a', 'assumes': 'mu-g3-choose', 'hands_on': 'mu-g5-choose', 'model_in': 'listening-log', 'model_out': 'listening-log', 'words': 'technical skill; setting; context; reflect; choose; explain', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Choose a piece for the class to perform and argue for it (interest, what the class can play, where it will be heard), and tell what in the student's own experience the pick reflects. What changes: the child's own technical skill is a reason for choosing, where grade 3 weighed setting. Assessed by a listening-log entry with a reason scored on a short rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '4', 'skill_id': 'mu-g4-respond', 'standard': 'MU:Re7.2.4a; MU:Re9.1.4a; MU:Cn11.1.4a', 'assumes': 'mu-g3-respond', 'hands_on': 'mu-g5-respond', 'model_in': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'model_out': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'words': 'structure; element; culture; criteria; explain; connect', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Listen to a piece, describe how its form, elements and social or cultural setting shape the response, score it with set criteria and say whether it fits its setting, and link it to another art or subject. What changes: explaining replaces describing: the child says why the setting changes the response. Assessed by a listen-and-explain response scored on a short rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'mu-g5-invent', 'standard': 'MU:Cr1.1.5a; MU:Cr1.1.5b', 'assumes': 'mu-g4-invent', 'hands_on': 'mu-g6-invent', 'model_in': 'idea-bank', 'model_out': 'idea-bank', 'words': 'context; culture; history; chords; accompaniment; society', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Improvise rhythm, melody and harmony, explain the tie between the ideas and a social, cultural or historical setting, and invent an accompaniment with easy chords. What changes: ideas are tied to a social, cultural or historical setting, and easy chords back them. Assessed by a performance and a short explanation with one piece of evidence, scored on a rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'mu-g5-document', 'standard': 'MU:Cr2.1.5a; MU:Cr2.1.5b', 'assumes': 'mu-g4-document', 'hands_on': 'mu-g6-document', 'model_in': 'notation-ladder', 'model_out': 'notation-ladder', 'words': 'developed; two-chord; arrange; context; notation; recording', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Develop ideas for an improvisation, arrangement or short composition, say what each is for, and notate the rhythm, the melody and a two-chord harmony. What changes: ideas are developed further and a two-chord harmony is written, where grade 4 wrote a simple harmony part. Assessed by a documented piece, played with its purpose and setting explained, scored on a rubric for development and clear notation.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'mu-g5-revise', 'standard': 'MU:Cr3.1.5a; MU:Cr3.2.5a', 'assumes': 'mu-g4-revise', 'hands_on': 'mu-g6-revise', 'model_in': 'critique-protocol', 'model_out': 'critique-protocol', 'words': 'reasons; criteria; revise; well-crafted; audience; growth', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Revise a piece against shared criteria, logging each change with its reason, then share the polished version with an audience and explain how it shows the student's aim. What changes: the child explains why each change was made. Assessed by a portfolio entry with before and after versions and reasons, shared with an audience with its intent explained, scored on a rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'mu-g5-read', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.2.5a; MU:Pr4.2.5b', 'assumes': 'mu-g4-read', 'hands_on': 'mu-g6-read', 'model_in': 'rhythm-syllables', 'model_out': 'rhythm-syllables', 'words': 'harmony; timing; pitch; form; staff; notation', 'cross_subject': 'math:5.NF.A.1 (adding mixed note values within a bar)', 'notes': 'Show how timing, pitch, form and harmony work in a piece chosen to perform, and read and perform it from standard notation. Mixed note values are added within a bar. What changes: harmony joins the elements and standard notation is now the default, where grade 4 used picture or standard notation. Assessed by a read-and-play task and a written explanation scored on a rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'mu-g5-express', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.3.5a; MU:Re8.1.5a', 'assumes': 'mu-g4-express', 'hands_on': 'mu-g6-express', 'model_in': 'expression-map', 'model_out': 'expression-map', 'words': 'articulation; tone color; interpretive choice; intent; explain; performer', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Plan the dynamics, tempo, tone color and articulation of a piece on an expression map and perform it, then explain how a recorded performer's choices carry the music's meaning. What changes: articulation joins the qualities explained, where grade 4 explained tone color. Assessed by a performance and a written explanation scored on a rubric."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'mu-g5-perform', 'standard': 'MU:Pr5.1.5a; MU:Pr5.1.5b; MU:Pr6.1.5a; MU:Pr6.1.5b', 'assumes': 'mu-g4-perform', 'hands_on': 'mu-g6-perform', 'model_in': 'practice-plan', 'model_out': 'practice-plan', 'words': 'growth; criteria; genre; style; interpretation; venue', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': "Rehearse a piece against the teacher's checklist across several weeks, keeping takes that show growth, and perform alone or in a group with manners that fit the style, genre and venue. What changes: growth over time is shown across rehearsals with a log, where grade 4 judged by shared criteria. Assessed by a performance, takes judged on the teacher's criteria and a rehearsal log, with performer and audience manners observed, scored on a rubric. Teacher note: a solo or doubled version is always offered."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'mu-g5-choose', 'standard': 'MU:Pr4.1.5a; MU:Re7.1.5a; MU:Cn10.1.5a', 'assumes': 'mu-g4-choose', 'hands_on': 'mu-g6-choose', 'model_in': 'listening-log', 'model_out': 'listening-log', 'words': 'evidence; interest; skill; setting; context; choose', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Choose a piece to perform, weighing interest, what the student and others can play and where it will be heard, and back the choice with evidence of what it reflects. What changes: claims come with evidence from the music. Assessed by a listening-log entry with evidence scored on a rubric.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '5', 'skill_id': 'mu-g5-respond', 'standard': 'MU:Re7.2.5a; MU:Re9.1.5a; MU:Cn11.1.5a; MU:Pr4.2.5c', 'assumes': 'mu-g4-respond', 'hands_on': 'mu-g6-respond', 'model_in': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'model_out': 'describe-interpret-judge', 'words': 'evidence; history; culture; criteria; setting; connect', 'cross_subject': 'ela:W.4.1 (an opinion supported by reasons, taught the year before)', 'notes': "Write a short response to a piece backed by evidence from the music: how its form, elements and setting shape the student's reaction, how it scores on set criteria for fit to its setting, and how history and culture shape its performance, then link it to another art, subject or setting. What changes: evidence from the music is required, in the response and in the judgment, and the setting of a performance is tied to history and society. Assessed by a written response with evidence scored on a rubric. Teacher note: A sacred or ceremonial work is used only when its source says it is open to be taught, and never as an exercise, warm-up, costume or imitation; any cultural claim is checked against a source before a unit names it."}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '6', 'skill_id': 'mu-g6-invent', 'standard': 'MU:Cr1.1.6a', 'assumes': 'mu-g5-invent', 'hands_on': 'mu-g7-invent', 'model_in': 'idea-bank', 'model_out': 'idea-bank', 'words': 'phrase; AB form; ABA form; intent; harmony; chord', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Compose short rhythm, melody and harmony phrases in AB or ABA form for a stated mood or aim. What changes: phrases are shaped into AB or ABA form to carry an intent. Assessed by a short composed piece scored on a rubric for form and intent.'}
{'strand': 'mu', 'grade': '6', 'skill_id': 'mu-g6-document', 'standard': 'MU:Cr2.1.6a; MU:Cr2.1.6b', 'assumes': 'mu-g5-document', 'hands_on': 'mu-g7-document', 'model_in': 'notation-ladder', 'model_out': 'notation-ladder', 'words': 'AB form; ABA form; beginning; middle; end; two chords', 'cross_subject': '', 'notes': 'Notate an AB or ABA piece with a clear start, middle and end, using two-chord harmony and simple rhythm and melody phrases. What changes: pieces have a planned shape from start to finish, where grade 5 documented developed ideas. Assessed by a documented piece scored on a rubric for shape and clear notation or audio.'}
