docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:397:## The bar and the approach, criterion by criterion
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:401:### Arts part (criteria 1 to 9)
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:405:| 1 All four artistic processes in each course | Part | APPROACH "Practices": "Over a year every course touches all four processes." Connecting has no day (finding 21). |
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:406:| 2 Technique taught directly, in steps, gets harder | Part | "What the arts carry": "taught in steps that get harder"; "Practice that returns": "at a harder step." No fading and no model holder (finding 5). |
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:407:| 3 Discipline's words taught and used in making and responding | Pass | "A study day ends with a sentence that must use one of the day's words"; "words come back in every response." (EL depth is finding 8.) |
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:410:| 6 Feedback given and received; reflect to refine | Fail | No critique protocol; revision only on a Respond day after the check (finding 10). |
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:411:| 7 Works from many times and cultures, with history and setting taught | Part | "From more than one time and culture across the year, each with its setting taught." No setting definition, no living artists, no sacred-work or imitation rule, no record (findings 12, 13). |
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:412:| 8 Assessment ranges: guide-scored work, self-assessment, work kept over time | Part | Guide, self-check, portfolio all named. Guide design, samples, check-day logistics, baseline and growth missing (finding 11). |
