docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:449:## Pointers to what a progression writer would get wrong from these pages
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:451:- Count ids by grade wrongly (finding 2): header "per grade" figures are unlettered standards; music and theater K are uneven.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:452:- Quote the performance standards' verbs (finding 1) or not know what an id asks.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:454:- Teach a note-value unit before the math week, or reteach fractions (finding 20).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:455:- Treat "respond" as the process on a respond day (finding 22).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:456:- Assume 160 course days in arts K to 8 because of the old note (finding 4).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:458:## Settled by the expert
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:470:## What is right and should not be touched
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:472:- The standard file itself: edition, header, per-discipline counts and the note that the high school music strand is a separate load.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:474:- The decision to claim composition and theory only for high school music and to leave ensemble, harmonizing instrument and technology strands out, with an ensemble companion page.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:480:## For Cory
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:485:2. **High school short path.** Recommended: yes, add an 80-day path to every high school level so a rotation or semester school can run it (finding 17). Alternative: leave levels as 160 daily sessions and accept the bar's "daily period" fail-if on those four years of five disciplines. This adds build scope to 15 courses of 160 days.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:486:3. **A "what a school may leave out" statement per arts course.** Recommended: yes (finding 12): dance, theater, masks and play-acting units each stand alone, so a school or family that objects can omit one without breaking the course. This is the same stance Cory took for health's sensitive units.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-read-2026-11-19.md:487:4. **Approach yes.** Recommended: no yes until findings 4 to 16 are applied; then yes. It is a draft and not in force.
