docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:11:## Verdict
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:13:The arts pre-work is much stronger after the 2026-11-19 fixes: the 1,114 own-words lines are cleanly paraphrased, the K to 8 band-year rule and high school composition-and-theory music choice are sound, and the five day kinds and ordinary-room rules fit Curio Class. The biggest risk is that stage 2 and stage 4 writers will hit hard contradictions between the prose and the gates: a likely phantom duplicate id (`MU:Re9.1.Kb`), an unstated `grade`-column mapping for high school levels alongside a `code_grades` rule that blocks every K to 8 and Level 1 `~` carry, missing core progression skill ids in every cross-subject lean, and an `APPROACH.md` that still omits or misplaces half of `UNIT-PLAN.md`'s unit and section fields. The one change that matters most before stage 2 and stage 3 build on these pages is reconciling `STANDARD.md` with `scripts/progression.py` (ownership, `~` carry, high school `.C` music ids, and the 12-day bridge rule) while completing the missing `UNIT-PLAN.md` field map in `APPROACH.md`.
