docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:30:## Findings, most serious first
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:32:### 1. Likely phantom duplicate id `MU:Re9.1.Kb` and `MU:Cn10.1`/`Cn11.1` vs official `MU:Cn10.0`/`Cn11.0` in the standards files
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:36:  1. `MU:Re9.1.Kb` appears in `ncas-performance-standards.txt` (line 700), making kindergarten the only grade in PK to 8 with two `Re9.1` statements (PK and grades 1 to 8 all have `a` only). In `ncas-performance-standards-words.txt` (lines 635 to 636), `MU:Re9.1.Ka` and `MU:Re9.1.Kb` carry the exact same wording ("With help, judge music by taste and expression."). Web search against the published National Core Arts Standards for Kindergarten Music (`nationalartsstandards.org` and NAfME) shows only `MU:Re9.1.Ka` ("With guidance, apply personal and expressive preferences in the evaluation of music."). Because header line 15 of `ncas-performance-standards.txt` notes that letters were derived by parsing the PDF cell layout rather than copied from a published list, `MU:Re9.1.Kb` is almost certainly a parsing artifact. If removed after checking the 2021-11 PDF, music K drops from 19 to 18, taught music ids from 185 to 184, taught total from 1,114 to 1,113, and file total from 1,202 to 1,201.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:37:  2. Official 2014 NCAS Music Connecting standards are coded `MU:Cn10.0` and `MU:Cn11.0` (for example `MU:Cn10.0.Ka`, `MU:Cn10.0.8a`, `MU:Cn10.0.C.Ia`, `MU:Cn11.0.Ka`), whereas the other four disciplines use `.1`. Curio Class's files use `MU:Cn10.1.*` and `MU:Cn11.1.*` (20 ids across PK to 8) without recording a `.0 -> .1` normalization in header line 18 of `ncas-performance-standards.txt`. Also, in `ncas-performance-standards-words.txt`, all nine grades K to 8 carry the exact same sentence for `MU:Cn10.1` and the exact same sentence for `MU:Cn11.1` (reflecting NCAS's overarching connecting statements), giving writers no grade-by-grade depth ladder for music connecting.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:39:- **Cost:** A kindergarten music scope and sequence will plan and assess a non-existent standard (`MU:Re9.1.Kb`), or fail a future id-existence check against the official framework. External reviewers checking music connecting codes against official NCAS tables will see `.1` where NCAS publishes `.0`.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:41:  1. Re-open the 2021-11 `Music at a Glance.pdf` cell for Kindergarten `Re9.1`. If only `a.` exists, delete `MU:Re9.1.Kb` from both `ncas-performance-standards.txt` and `ncas-performance-standards-words.txt`, and update the counts in `STANDARD.md` section 1 and section 3.2 (1,201 total, 1,113 taught, music 201 total / 184 taught, music K to 2 = `18 + 20 + 20 = 58`).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:42:  2. Check `MU:Cn10.0` / `MU:Cn11.0` in the same PDF. Either change the 20 codes in both files to `.0` (both `scripts/standards.py` line 107 and `scripts/progression.py` line 121 already accept `\.\d\.`) or add `MU:Cn10.0/Cn11.0 -> Cn10.1/Cn11.1` to header line 18 of `ncas-performance-standards.txt`. Add one line to `STANDARD.md` section 3.1 noting that NCAS Music `Cn10` and `Cn11` share one overarching wording across K to 8, so each grade teaches them at that grade's repertoire and vocabulary depth.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:45:- **Confidence:** Firm on the duplicate wording in `words.txt`, the 15-word line, and the official `MU:Cn10.0`/`Cn11.0` notation; Likely on `MU:Re9.1.Kb` being absent from the 2021-11 PDF (confirmed by web search summaries, PDF itself not opened).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:47:### 2. Ownership and handoff rules do not match `scripts/progression.py`, and four gaps block Stage 2
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:53:  3. **The 63 high school music `.C` ids are not loaded in `ncas-performance-standards.txt`.** `STANDARD.md` 1 and 3.3 defer loading them until "the high school music frame is written" (Stage 3). Because `STD_FILES['arts']` reads `ncas-performance-standards.txt`, `scripts/progression.py` (Stage 2) cannot accept any high school music standard code (even though `code_grades` line 121 already has `(?:C\.)?` ready for them). That either blocks high school music rows in `data/progressions/arts.csv` or leaves music ending at grade 8 in the progression.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:54:  4. **The Level 1 bridge rule contradicts "assumes no earlier arts learning" and leaves the Grade 8 to Level 1 handoff ambiguous.** Line 103 says "Level 1's first unit assumes no earlier arts learning." Line 110 says "Level 1 opens with a bridge unit of at most 12 days that teaches the discipline's grade 8 ids". Teaching and checking all 15 to 24 grade 8 ids (24 in theater, 21 in dance and music) in 12 days is impossible alongside making, critique, showing and respond, and claiming to "teach" grade 8 ids blurs ownership. `STANDARD.md` also never states whether Grade 8 `hands_on` to Level 1 (`9`) in the progression or how Level 1's `assumes` column handles students entering with no K to 8 arts.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:55:- **Cost:** Stage 2 progression writers cannot write compliant high school rows for music or `~` return rows for any discipline without failing `scripts/progression.py`, and Stage 3 writers will build an impossible 12-day bridge unit trying to cover 24 grade 8 ids.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:61:  In `scripts/progression.py` `code_grades('arts', code)`, extend `all_grades` (second element of the returned tuple) to allow `~` in the immediately next grade/level (`K`->`1`, ..., `8`->`9`, `9`->`10`, `10`->`11`, `11`->`12`) while keeping `owner_grades` strictly `[g]` / `[LEVEL[g]]`. Load the 63 `.C` high school music ids into `ncas-performance-standards.txt` and `ncas-performance-standards-words.txt` now rather than waiting for Stage 3 (see Questions for Cory 2).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:64:### 3. `APPROACH.md` omits or misplaces half of `UNIT-PLAN.md`'s unit and section fields, and disagrees with the bar on where works and showing live
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:91:| Section 11 Not in this section, and still to make | Missing | Not named (needed for dance/PE, music/math, media arts/CS boundaries and "from memory" marks) |
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:102:> - **Unit field 5 (End-of-unit assessment, whole):** The showing or performance guide (three to five look-fors scored met, partly or not yet, never talent, neatness, effort or comparison), or an unseen-work response (visual arts: CC0 image; music: public domain audio or Curio Class playback; media arts: public domain image/clip or Curio Class original; dance and theater: short written description, live teacher demonstration or Curio Class original, never an embed). Two sample descriptions or adult-made examples per open task. Accommodations line: oral or shown response, large-print step card, seated or one-limb version, live observation in place of recording, extra time.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:121:> - **Section field 11 (Not in this section, and still to make):** Boundaries with other subjects (dance/PE, music/math, media arts/CS), spec-only tools, and every "from memory" mark the plan relies on.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:125:### 4. Cross-subject leans in `STANDARD.md` section 6 name no core progression skill ids
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:128:- **What is wrong:** Section 6 lists six cross-subject leans (music/math fractions, visual arts/math geometry and ratio, theater/ELA reading literature and speaking/listening plus claim-and-evidence writing, dance/PE `SHAPE.S1`, media arts/CS privacy and copyright, all arts/social studies sourcing habits). None of the six names a single `skill_id` from `data/progressions/math.csv`, `ela.csv`, `social-studies.csv`, `physical-education.csv` or `computer-science.csv` (only one broad standard strand, `SHAPE.S1`, is given).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:131:  > - **Music and math:** beat, note values and measures lean on grade 3 and 4 fraction rows (`<math skill_id>`, `<math skill_id>`). A music unit on note values is placed after the math week that teaches those rows (`data/plans/calendar.csv`), or uses beat counts only.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:134:### 5. Course list, `core` flags, and high school course count are inconsistent across `STANDARD.md` and `data/courses.csv`
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:138:  1. `STANDARD.md` line 5 and `ADOPTION-BAR-SUBJECTS.md` lines 214 and 563 state **20 courses** (five disciplines by four bands: K to 2, 3 to 5, 6 to 8, 9 to 12). `data/courses.csv` still has only **5** rows (`visual-arts`, `music`, `theater`, `dance`, `media-arts`), all with `grades = k-12` (whereas SEL and ELD were updated on 2026-11-21 to four band rows each: `sel-k-2` to `sel-9-12`, `eld-k-2` to `eld-9-12`).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:139:  2. In `data/courses.csv` lines 28 and 29, `visual-arts` and `music` have `core = y`, while `ADOPTION-BAR-SUBJECTS.md` lines 8 to 9 and `PRODUCTION-PATH.md` define the four core subjects as math, ELA, science and social studies (arts are later subjects).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:140:  3. `STANDARD.md` line 113 says: "The short path adds build work to **the 15 high school courses**". That contradicts line 5 ("20 courses, five disciplines by four bands"), line 100 ("The 9 to 12 band is one course per discipline, as every other band is; its years are levels"), and line 131 ("High school music is one of the 20 courses, not an extra one"). Five disciplines by three levels is **15 high school levels** (inside 5 high school courses), not 15 courses.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:142:- **Cost:** Downstream scripts (`frame.py`, `course_status.py`, `plan.py`) and stage 3 frame writers will disagree on whether arts has 5, 20, or 30 courses, whether visual arts and music belong in core-course builds, and how frame slugs are named.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:149:### 6. Dose by band omits high school minutes per lesson and cites no K to 8 national/professional body time figures
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:155:     - **NAfME** (Music OTL Standards): at least **90 minutes per week** of general music for every student through grade 8. Curio Class's 64-day K to 8 default (2 x 40 = 80 min/week) is slightly below it, and the 32-day short path (40 min/week) is under half.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:158:     - **EdTA** (Theatre OTL Standards): at least **45 minutes/day for at least one semester each year** in middle school (about 60 to 67.5 hours/year, vs Curio Class's 42.7 hours/year at 64 x 40 min); elementary scheduling comparable to music and visual arts.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:163:  > **Published professional time figures (K to 8).** National arts associations publish Opportunity-to-Learn targets: NAfME recommends at least 90 minutes per week of general music through grade 8; NAEA recommends at least 50 minutes per week in elementary visual arts and grade-level sequential courses in middle school; NDEO recommends 30 minutes per day, 3 to 5 days per week in elementary dance and 40 to 60 minutes per day, 3 to 5 days per week in middle school; EdTA recommends at least 45 minutes per day for one semester each year in middle school theatre. Curio Class's K to 8 default (64 sessions of 40 minutes, 80 minutes per week, about 42.7 hours a year) meets NAEA's elementary floor and sits below the music, dance and middle-school theatre targets; the 32-session short path (40 minutes per week) sits below all four. Each course page names the relevant association figure and the gap so a school can add sessions where its schedule allows.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:166:### 7. Sensitive ground misses four arts-specific risks, has no disclosure/reporting route, and leaves the unit leave-out rule contradictory
