docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:234:## Questions for Cory
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:236:1. **Catalogue grain and `core` flag in `data/courses.csv` (Finding 5).** `data/courses.csv` still has 5 K to 12 arts rows, with `visual-arts` and `music` marked `core = y`. **Recommended:** replace the 5 rows with 20 band rows (5 disciplines by 4 bands, matching `sel-*` and `eld-*`), set `core = n` on all 20, and confirm the Stage 3 frame grain (45 K to 8 grade-year frames plus 15 Level 1 to 3 frames and optional Level 4 frames).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:237:2. **Load the 63 high school music `.C` ids now vs at Stage 3 (Finding 2).** Leaving them out of `ncas-performance-standards.txt` prevents `scripts/progression.py` from gating high school music in Stage 2. **Recommended:** load the 63 `.C` ids and their 63 own-words lines into both files now, before Stage 2 closes.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:238:3. **High school session length and K to 8 OTL time figures (Finding 6).** High school levels imply 45 minutes a day (160 x 45 min = 120 hours) but state no minute figure; K to 8 cites no professional body figures. **Recommended:** lock 45 minutes for grades 9 to 12 (120 hours full, 60 hours short path), keep 40 minutes for K to 8 (64 / 32 days), and publish the NAfME, NAEA, NDEO and EdTA OTL figures with the gap noted plainly on each course page (as health does).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:239:4. **Level 1 bridge unit (12 days) vs "teaches the discipline's grade 8 ids" (Finding 2).** Teaching all 15 to 24 grade 8 ids in 12 days is not feasible and blurs ownership. **Recommended:** define the 12-day bridge as foundational readiness for Level 1 (key K to 8 techniques and vocabulary carried as `~` readiness, not a claim to teach and assess all grade 8 ids), with Level 1 claiming `.I` ids only.
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:240:5. **Leaving out a whole unit vs C1 (Finding 7).** `STANDARD.md` section 5 says a school may leave out a unit and "the standards are still met elsewhere in the year." **Recommended:** distinguish leaving out a *work* (swap another work; standards still met) from leaving out a *unit* (the course page and family note state which standard ids are then not claimed for that year, matching the SEL rule).
docs/reviews\prework-arts-gemini-2026-11-20.md:241:6. **Confirming and removing `MU:Re9.1.Kb` (and `.0` vs `.1` on `MU:Cn10`/`Cn11`) (Finding 1).** **Recommended:** verify against the 2021-11 `Music at a Glance.pdf`, remove `MU:Re9.1.Kb` if it is a parsing duplicate (changing taught count from 1,114 to 1,113 and music K from 19 to 18), and either use official `.0` on `MU:Cn10`/`Cn11` or document the normalization in the file header.
